.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_VARIANT 3 2026-11-04 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_variant \- enumerate exact stored filename identities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>

int32_t libmpq__file_variant(
        mpq_archive_s *archive, const char *filename,
        uint32_t variant_index, mpq_file_identity_s *identity);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enumerate live identities for filename using a zero-based ordinal. Classic
probing continues across deleted slots, stopping at the first never-used slot
or full wrap. Results follow ascending original hash-slot order, including
wraparound chains. Slots themselves are not public persistent identifiers.
Aliases may share a canonical file number; locale/platform variants are not
deduplicated. Duplicate identities are rejected even if they share a member.
.PP
The naturally aligned 16-byte mpq_file_identity_s contains uint32_t
file_number and flags, uint16_t locale and platform, then uint32_t reserved.
Offsets are 0, 4, 8, 10 and 12 respectively. Reserved is always zero.
LIBMPQ_IDENTITY_CLASSIC and LIBMPQ_IDENTITY_BET report stored provenance,
not file-storage flags. Reconciled mixed entries can carry both bits.
.PP
A HET/BET-only match returns one unqualified BET identity with zero selectors.
Validated classic variants take precedence in mixed archives. No duplicate
BET variant is added. Exact extended lookup requires full normalized 64-bit
HET/56-bit BET hashes, a unique mapping and names of at most 264 bytes.
Ambiguous or incomplete mappings are rejected, without filename recovery.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success or a negative libmpq error. A valid output is entirely
cleared on failure. No partial stream is returned.
.SH ERRORS
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates missing required arguments, an absent identity
or the end of enumeration. LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT indicates malformed canonical
mappings, contradictory duplicate identities or unsupported reduced hashes.
Read-only identity queries reject writable archives with
LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED. Stream opening rejects invalid writer handles
with LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. Existing allocation, source I/O and decode errors
are propagated. All source archives remain unchanged.
